,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406220571,"data":"# Phase 5 results: does the yardstick matter?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406223922,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406227105,"data":"Each experiment trains one model and keeps the epoch with the best validation score.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406230562,"data":"The two differ almost only in what that validation set measures:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.40623395,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406237083,"data":"- **A** validates on unseen compounds AND unseen proteins, built like the test set.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406240562,"data":"- **B** validates on random pairs whose compounds and proteins were all seen in training\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.40624389,"data":"  (the Phase 3 / paper style). B trains on ~7% fewer rows; everything else is identical.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406247249,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406250323,"data":"| Experiment | What its validation measures | Stopped at epoch | Validation MSE | Test MSE | Test CI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.40625381,"data":"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406256948,"data":"| davis_A | new yardstick: validation is unseen compounds and proteins | 102 of 150 | 0.514 | **0.644** | 0.610 |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406260447,"data":"| davis_B | control: validation is random pairs, all entities seen | 83 of 150 | 0.425 | **0.697** | 0.574 |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406263781,"data":"| metz_A | new yardstick: validation is unseen compounds and proteins | 81 of 150 | 0.727 | **0.759** | 0.655 |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406267042,"data":"| metz_B | control: validation is random pairs, all entities seen | 146 of 150 | 0.532 | **0.719** | 0.640 |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.40627185,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406288284,"data":"\u003e The validation MSE columns are **not comparable between A and B**: they are measured\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406291092,"data":"\u003e on different sets. A validates on a harder, unseen-entity set, so its number is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406293384,"data":"\u003e expected to be higher even if its model is better. Compare the test column.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406295678,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406297834,"data":"## Against Phase 4 and the paper\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406300056,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406302236,"data":"| Dataset | Phase 4 test MSE | Phase 5 A | Phase 5 B | Paper (5-fold) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406304543,"data":"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406306764,"data":"| Davis | 0.716 | 0.644 | 0.697 | 0.463 |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406309183,"data":"| Metz | 0.762 | 0.759 | 0.719 | 0.658 |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406311484,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406313581,"data":"Phase 4 trained on more rows than either run here (novel-pair validation wastes the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406315995,"data":"mixed pairs), so a Phase 5 run matching Phase 4 is already an improvement per training row.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18425.406359597,"data":"\n"}
